# bat's configuration.
#
# Only the syntax theme lives here, and only as a fallback. BAT_THEME in
# ~/.zshenv and ~/.bashrc-custom is still the source of truth — bat reads the
# environment variable in preference to this file, so setting it there
# continues to decide what bat, delta and the yazi preview all show.
#
# What this file buys is the case where there is no environment to read: bat
# launched from something that is not one of those shells — an editor task, a
# GUI app, a cron job, `env -i` — otherwise falls back to bat's own default
# (Monokai Extended), which looks nothing like the rest of the setup. Same
# reasoning as vendoring btop's theme rather than trusting the packaged copy,
# and as keeping ~/.config/lf/colors even though lf reads LS_COLORS.
#
# tests/check-theme.py checks that every file naming this theme names the
# same one. Palette reference: docs/tokyonight.md
--theme="Visual Studio Dark+"
